WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:18.160
The Winkies were very grateful to Dorothy and her friends so they gave them many gifts.

2
00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:21.622
They gave the Lion and Toto gold collars.

3
00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:26.439
They gave the Tin Man a gold-handled ax and a jewel-covered oilcan.

4
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:32.479
They gave the Scarecrow a walking stick with a gold handle, and they gave Dorothy a gold bracelet.

5
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.583
It had jewels to match the golden hat she had taken after the Witch melted.

6
00:00:37.584 --> 00:00:40.945
The journey back to Oz was long and difficult.

7
00:00:40.946 --> 00:00:46.597
The Winged Monkeys had flown the Tin Man and Scarecrow a great distance before dropping them.

8
00:00:46.598 --> 00:00:50.544
Dorothy and the Lion had been taken all the way to the castle.

9
00:00:50.545 --> 00:00:56.287
They followed the rising sun, but then it became cloudy and the sun was gone.

10
00:00:56.288 --> 00:01:00.565
It remained cloudy for several days, but the group continued.

11
00:01:00.566 --> 00:01:04.054
"We have lost our way," said the Scarecrow.

12
00:01:04.055 --> 00:01:08.940
"If we walk far enough," said Dorothy, "we will arrive somewhere."

13
00:01:08.941 --> 00:01:12.839
The others didn't look hopeful.

14
00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.722
"Let's call the field mice," suggested the Tin Man.

15
00:01:16.723 --> 00:01:20.964
"Why didn't we think of that before?" asked the Scarecrow.

16
00:01:20.965 --> 00:01:24.710
Dorothy took out the Witch's silver whistle and blew.

17
00:01:24.711 --> 00:01:30.502
Soon many gray field mice, as well as the Queen herself, arrived.

18
00:01:30.503 --> 00:01:33.688
"How can we help you?" asked the Queen.

19
00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:38.343
"We are lost," answered Dorothy. "How do we get to Oz?"

20
00:01:38.344 --> 00:01:41.349
"It is quite far," replied the Queen.

21
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.546
"Because you've been walking in the wrong direction.

22
00:01:44.547 --> 00:01:47.856
It will take you many days to reach Oz.

23
00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:52.860
Why don't you call the Winged Monkeys to take you there?"

24
00:01:52.861 --> 00:01:57.602
"The Winged Monkeys?" asked Dorothy, not understanding the Queen.

25
00:01:57.603 --> 00:02:03.841
"You are wearing the golden hat so you can command the Winged Monkeys," said the Queen.

26
00:02:03.842 --> 00:02:06.380
"But how?" asked Dorothy.

27
00:02:06.381 --> 00:02:12.419
"The directions are inside the hat," answered the Queen.

28
00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:18.850
After reading the directions, Dorothy put the hat back on her head and stood with her feet apart.

29
00:02:18.851 --> 00:02:23.376
She raised her hands above her head and said, "By my command!"

30
00:02:23.377 --> 00:02:32.187
The magic of the hat changed Dorothy's voice, and the sound scared her and her friends.

31
00:02:32.188 --> 00:02:38.106
The King of the Monkeys bowed before Dorothy and asked, "What is your command?"

32
00:02:38.107 --> 00:02:42.190
"We wish to go to the Emerald City," said Dorothy.

33
00:02:42.191 --> 00:02:45.304
"We will carry you," replied the King.

34
00:02:45.305 --> 00:02:52.259
The Monkeys quickly obeyed Dorothy's command, and soon they were flying toward Oz.

35
00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.674
"Why must you obey me?" asked Dorothy.

36
00:02:55.675 --> 00:03:01.113
"It is our punishment," replied the King. "We made mischief on a princess.

37
00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:04.926
Her husband gave the golden hat to her on her wedding day.

38
00:03:04.927 --> 00:03:08.679
She used the hat to order us out of her kingdom."

39
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:13.060
"How did the Wicked Witch get the hat?" asked Dorothy.

40
00:03:13.061 --> 00:03:18.530
"We don't know," said the King. "But she made us do terrible things.

41
00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:23.760
We enslaved the Winkies and drove Oz himself out of the Land of the West.

42
00:03:23.761 --> 00:03:29.736
Then she ordered us to kill you, but we couldn't because of the Good Witch's kiss."

43
00:03:29.737 --> 00:03:35.023
"Look!" shouted Dorothy. "There's the Emerald City."

44
00:03:35.024 --> 00:03:39.606
The Winged Monkeys left Dorothy and her friends at the Emerald City's gate.

45
00:03:39.607 --> 00:03:44.689
Dorothy and her friends thanked them for the ride, and the Winged Monkeys flew away.

46
00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:54.151
"Now we will get what we have been promised," said the Scarecrow happily, and they rang the bell.

47
00:03:54.152 --> 00:03:59.297
"What! Back again?" asked the gatekeeper in surprise.

48
00:03:59.298 --> 00:04:03.941
"You see us, so you know we are here," said the Tin Man.

49
00:04:03.942 --> 00:04:08.617
"But you went to visit the Witch," he replied.

50
00:04:08.618 --> 00:04:12.229
"We did visit her," said the Lion.

51
00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:17.351
"And she let you go?" the gatekeeper asked in disbelief.

52
00:04:17.352 --> 00:04:23.125
"She melted, so we were free to go," answered the Scarecrow.

53
00:04:23.126 --> 00:04:27.683
"She melted? Who melted her?" the gatekeeper asked.

54
00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:31.681
"I did, sir," said Dorothy quietly.

55
00:04:31.682 --> 00:04:37.951
"My goodness!" the gatekeeper exclaimed. "Well, come in. Come in."

56
00:04:37.952 --> 00:04:44.323
While the gatekeeper placed special eyeglasses on the visitors, a large crowd gathered.

57
00:04:44.324 --> 00:04:50.646
News of the Witch's death had spread fast, and everyone wanted to see what Oz would give to the heroes.

58
00:04:50.647 --> 00:04:58.490
The soldier went and spoke to Oz, but Oz did not see them that day.

59
00:04:58.491 --> 00:05:02.264
Dorothy and her friends returned to their former rooms and waited.

60
00:05:02.265 --> 00:05:06.573
Many days passed and Oz still did not summon them.

61
00:05:06.574 --> 00:05:10.507
Tired of waiting, Dorothy and her friends sent a message to Oz:

62
00:05:10.508 --> 00:05:21.995
If you do not see us, we will call the Winged Monkeys and tell them to destroy the Emerald City.
